---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="A bit about who I am — lektor, former space technologist, occasional tinkerer."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">

    <!-- Page heading -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text)">About</h1>
      <p class="text-lg" style="color: var(--color-muted)">
        <!--
          TODO: One-liner intro. Keep it plain.
          Example: "Teacher. Reader. Reluctant gardener-adjacent."
        -->
        Teacher. Reader. Reluctant gardener-adjacent.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Avatar placeholder -->
    <div class="mb-10">
      <!--
        TODO: Replace with your own photo.
        Drop a photo at /public/avatar.jpg and uncomment the <img> below.
      -->
      <img
        src="/avatar.jpg"
        alt="Photo of Sigurd"
        class="w-28 h-28 rounded-full border-2 object-cover"
        style="border-color: var(--color-accent)"
      />
      <!--
      <div
        class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full border-2 flex items-center justify-center text-3xl font-bold"
        style="border-color: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-card)"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        S
      </div>
      -->
    </div>


    <!-- ── THE STORY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="prose-section mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4" style="color: var(--color-text)">
        The story, roughly
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-muted)">
        <p>
          <!--
            TODO: Write your own version here. Suggested tone: matter-of-fact.
            The details you gave me:

            - Master's in informatics
            - Former space technologist (worked with this at high-school level)
            - Now a lektor / teacher
            - AI enthusiast — uses it daily
            - Space enthusiast
            - Reader, loves books
            - Enjoys "vibe coding" — relaxed tinkering with small projects
            - Has a wife, kids, and a family garden (but he is not the gardener)
          -->
          I have a master’s degree in informatics. I once had a high-school qualification as a romteknolog — not exactly the glamorous astronaut kind, but the kind that involves a lot of data, a reasonable amount of patience, and the occasional satellite. In the end I didn’t chase that path. Instead I chose love, went with my now-wife to university, and studied informatics.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before settling into teaching I worked as a developer in a couple of companies and then spent two years as a game- and blockchain researcher in a small crypto/gaming startup. There I wrote around thirty research papers on tokenomics, blockchains and game economies.
        </p>
        <p>
          While doing that remote job I also completed my pedagogy education and became a father for the first time. It was a hectic couple of years, but somehow it all worked out.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since 2023 I’ve been teaching full-time at junior high on Lovund — math, science and English. It feels just right.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside of work I read quite a bit, follow space news, and whatever small project has caught my attention lately. We have a garden at home. My wife has the vision and the plans — I get dragged into the building part, and if I’m being honest I usually quite enjoy it too (though I won’t always admit that).
        </p>
        <p>
          I also enjoy living on Lovund with my family and tinkering and building software stuff — with AI making it all a lot more achievable.
        </p>
        <p>
          I use AI tools every day. At work for planning and feedback, at home for the small tinkering projects that would previously have required either more time or more skill than I had. I find the whole thing genuinely interesting in a low-key way — not as a hobby horse, more as a practical reality that is changing what a person with reasonable curiosity can actually get done.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’m also open to occasional side projects — especially simple web pages for companies or other interesting ideas. If you have something in mind, feel free to reach out.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- ── QUICK FACTS ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-6" style="color: var(--color-text)">
        Quick facts
      </h2>

      <dl class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {[
          { term: 'Role',       def: 'Lektor / Junior high teacher' },
          { term: 'Education',  def: 'Master\'s in informatics' },
          { term: 'Background', def: 'Systems Developer, Blockchain Researcher' },
          { term: 'Location',   def: 'Lovund, Norway' },
          { term: 'Interests',  def: 'AI, space, books, running, small software projects' },
          {
            term: 'Coding style',
            def: 'Slow, calm, AI-assisted — what I believe they call "vibe coding"',
          },
        ].map(({ term, def }) => (
          <div class="card p-4">
            <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-1" style="color: var(--color-accent)">{term}</dt>
            <dd class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-text)">{def}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </section>


    <!-- ── WHAT I USE / TOOLS ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4" style="color: var(--color-text)">
        Things I work with
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm mb-6" style="color: var(--color-muted)">
        <!--
          TODO: Replace or extend this list. Keep the tone understated.
          "I use X" is fine. "I am proficient in X at an expert level" is not.
        -->
        A non-exhaustive and probably already slightly out-of-date list.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {[
          'Python',
          'Django',
          'TypeScript',
          'JavaScript',
          'Astro',
          'Tailwind CSS',
          'SQL',
          'Git',
          'Linux',
          'Markdown',
          'Vercel',
          'Render',
          'Supabase',
          'AI tools (daily)',
          /* TODO: Add or remove technologies as appropriate */
        ].map(tech => (
          <span
            class="text-sm px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border font-mono"
            style="border-color: var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text); background: var(--color-card)"
          >
            {tech}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- ── CONTACT CTA ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="pt-8 border-t border-[var(--color-border)]">
      <p class="text-base mb-4" style="color: var(--color-muted)">
        <!--
          TODO: Short, casual contact invite. Or remove this section entirely
          if the Contact page handles it.
        -->
        If you have a question, a comment, or a book recommendation: feel free to get in touch.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-medium text-sm transition-all hover:opacity-90"
        style="background: var(--color-accent); color: #0f172a;"
      >
        Contact
      </a>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
